#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:30
msgid "A complete example file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:48
msgid "The two sections the engine never reads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:50
msgid ""
"The same file also configures `freeports-dev` and `freeports-validate`, "
"under two optional sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Both commands are only ever run by **format authors**. If you extract "
"data, these sections do not exist for you, and a file without them is "
"complete. {doc}`dev-and-validate` is their reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:65
msgid ""
"They live here rather than in two files of their own so that the settings"
" genuinely shared with the engine — `formats_repo`, `db_path` — stay at "
"the top level and get written **once**, for all three commands. The "
"engine parses the sections and then ignores them; parsing them at all is "
"what extends the unknown-key refusal below into `dev.tagret_lists`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:70
msgid "Relative paths in this file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:72
msgid ""
"A path written here is resolved against **the directory holding the "
"file**, not against the working directory the command happens to be run "
"from. That is the only reading that survives the way the file is found: "
"it is searched for — the working directory, then the user's, then the "
"system's — so one line is read from many different working directories "
"and has to name the same repository from all of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:83
msgid ""
"Paths given the other two ways keep the meaning they obviously have: "
"`--repo` on the command line and `FREEPORTS_FORMATS_REPO_PATH` in the "
"environment are relative to the shell you are standing in, because that "
"is where you typed them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:87
msgid ""
"The same rule reaches `validate.sources`, whose entries may be written as"
" bare paths rather than as URIs. A relative one is resolved against this "
"file's directory, for the same reason and with the same result — the "
"pages it names are the same pages from every working directory. A URI, "
"`file://` included, is left exactly as written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:93
msgid ""
"`freeports-validate` reads the file this way. The engine and `freeports-"
"dev` still resolve a relative path here against the working directory — "
"which is why a workspace configuration file tends to carry a comment "
"saying the run must start from its directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:98
msgid "The two grouped settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:100
msgid ""
"`parallelism` and `out_flags` are **maps with a closed set of sub-keys** "
"— two settings of one thing, grouped so the file reads as it thinks. Both"
" behave the same way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:103
msgid ""
"a sub-key left out stays **unset**, so another source still decides it. A"
" file naming only `archive` leaves `separate_out` alone;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:105
msgid ""
"an **unknown sub-key is an error naming its full path** — "
"`parallelism.pipelines`, `out_flags.compressed`. A level or a flag that "
"was considered and never implemented must not look active because a file "
"mentioned it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:108
msgid "a section that is not a map at all is an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:110
msgid ""
"Note that `out_flags.archive` is spelled as the flag is, not as the field"
" is: `compressed` is the internal name and is rejected here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:113
msgid "The file wants real YAML types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:114
msgid ""
"The file wants **real YAML types**, unlike the environment, which only "
"has strings: `save_pdf: true` is a boolean, not the string `\"true\"`. "
"Parallelism is the one place both are accepted, because YAML already "
"distinguishes `2` from `auto` and refusing a quoted number would be a "
"subtlety with no gain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:118
msgid "Unknown keys are errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:120
msgid ""
"At the top level as in the two sections. A misspelled key that is "
"silently ignored configures nothing and says nothing about it, and the "
"user is left believing a setting took effect. A file with a single "
"unknown key fails the run, naming the file and the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:124
msgid ""
"An empty file, or one holding nothing but `null`, contributes nothing and"
" is not an error. A top-level document that is not a mapping is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:127
msgid "Where the file is looked for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:129
msgid ""
"Unless `--config` names one, three tiers are searched in **decreasing** "
"precedence, and the first file found wins outright — the tiers do not "
"merge with each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:132
msgid ""
"**The working directory** — a file named, case-insensitively, `config-"
"freeports.yaml` or `freeports-config.yaml`, in their usual punctuation "
"and extension variants: a leading dot, `conf` for `config`, `-`, `_` or "
"`.` as separator, `.yml` for `.yaml`. This is the per-project "
"configuration, and the one to commit next to a batch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:136
msgid ""
"**The user tier** — the operating system's *local* configuration "
"directory, holding `freeports.yaml` or `freeports.yml`. Local rather than"
" roaming, deliberately: a file naming machine-local paths should not "
"follow you to another machine and point at directories that do not exist "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:140
msgid ""
"**The system tier** — the XDG configuration directories and then `/etc` "
"on POSIX; the program-data directory and then the system root on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:143
msgid ""
"No file anywhere is **not an error**. It simply means this layer "
"contributes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/config_file.md:145
msgid ""
"Both platform branches of the system tier are always compiled, whatever "
"the machine — which is how the tests exercise both regardless of which "
"system runs them."
msgstr ""

